["<aside class=\"callout why\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>The SKS (Simonov self loading carbine) can take a black tailed deer cleanly, inside a short range, with the right bullet. Outside that, it wounds.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart of energy in foot pounds: 7.62x39 123 grain soft point: 1508 at the muzzle, 1136 at 100 yards, 842 at 200 yards. .308 Winchester 150 grain: 2648, about 2090 at 100 m and 1630 at 200 m. A dashed line marks the 1,000 ft lb rule of thumb; the 7.62x39 drops under it past about 130 m.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Energy: 7.62x39 vs your .308</text>\n<line x1=\"30.0\" y1=\"252.0\" x2=\"380.0\" y2=\"252.0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"30.0\" y1=\"194.0\" x2=\"380.0\" y2=\"194.0\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/><line x1=\"70.0\" y1=\"76.0\" x2=\"96.0\" y2=\"76.0\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/><text x=\"102.0\" y=\"81.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"start\">1,000 ft lb rule of thumb</text><rect x=\"40.0\" y=\"164.5\" width=\"50.0\" height=\"87.5\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"94.0\" y=\"98.4\" width=\"50.0\" height=\"153.6\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#B9C4B0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"92.0\" y=\"270.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Muzzle</text><text x=\"65.0\" y=\"244.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1,508</text><text x=\"119.0\" y=\"244.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2,648</text><rect x=\"156.0\" y=\"186.1\" width=\"50.0\" height=\"65.9\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"210.0\" y=\"130.8\" width=\"50.0\" height=\"121.2\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#B9C4B0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"208.0\" y=\"270.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100 yd</text><text x=\"181.0\" y=\"244.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1,136</text><text x=\"235.0\" y=\"244.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2,090</text><rect x=\"272.0\" y=\"203.2\" width=\"50.0\" height=\"48.8\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"326.0\" y=\"157.5\" width=\"50.0\" height=\"94.5\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#B9C4B0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"324.0\" y=\"270.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">200 yd</text><text x=\"297.0\" y=\"244.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">842</text><text x=\"351.0\" y=\"244.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1,630</text><rect x=\"70.0\" y=\"44.0\" width=\"14.0\" height=\"14.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"90.0\" y=\"56.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">7.62x39 123 gr</text><rect x=\"230.0\" y=\"44.0\" width=\"14.0\" height=\"14.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#B9C4B0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"250.0\" y=\"56.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">.308 150 gr</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"288.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">SKS load in yards (Hornady). .308 in metres.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>7.62x39 has about half the energy of your .308 at 200 yd (180 m) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>It drops under the 1,000 ft lb rule of thumb past about 130 m (145 yd) (75%, computed).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the numbers</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Distance</th><th>7.62x39, Hornady 123 gr SST</th><th>.308, 150 gr (app table)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Muzzle</td><td>1,508 ft lb (2,045 J)</td><td>2,648 ft lb (3,590 J)</td></tr><tr><td>100</td><td>1,136 ft lb (1,540 J) at 100 yd</td><td>2,090 ft lb (2,840 J) at 100 m</td></tr><tr><td>200</td><td>842 ft lb (1,142 J) at 200 yd</td><td>1,630 ft lb (2,210 J) at 200 m</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>7.62x39: Hornady data, 20 inch test barrel, muzzle velocity 2,350 fps (feet per second) (75%, maker data via a retailer listing).</li><li>.308: from the app's <a href=\"#/s/ballistics-308/0\">.308 ballistics</a> lesson (75 to 85%).</li><li>Crossing 1,000 ft lb: about 146 yd, or 134 m, by straight line between Hornady's 100 and 200 yd figures (75%, Hunt Mentor arithmetic).</li><li>The 1,000 ft lb figure is a rule of thumb with no clear origin (70%, from the <a href=\"#/s/ballistics-deep/0\">ballistics deep dive</a>). Placement matters more <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>TC 9-56 lists a practical range of 400 m for soldiers <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. That is a military number, not a deer number.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 290\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Range rings around the hunter: 50 m, 100 m, and 150 m marked as your limit with the SKS. Most coastal deer shots are close (a Tip).\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"290\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">SKS deer range</text>\n<circle cx=\"200.0\" cy=\"260.0\" r=\"210.0\" fill=\"#DCE5D3\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"200.0\" cy=\"260.0\" r=\"150.0\" fill=\"#C9D8BE\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"200.0\" cy=\"260.0\" r=\"80.0\" fill=\"#B2C7A4\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"200.0\" cy=\"255.0\" r=\"8.0\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"196.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50 m</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"124.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100 m</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"44.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#B3261E\" text-anchor=\"middle\">150 m: your limit</text><text x=\"330.0\" y=\"230.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Most coastal</text><text x=\"330.0\" y=\"250.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">deer shots</text><text x=\"330.0\" y=\"270.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">are close (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Most coastal timber shots are close (Tip).</li><li>Your limit: 150 m (164 yd) with a soft point, and only if you pass the plate test (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why 150 m</summary><ul><li>Energy falls under the rule of thumb around 130 m (75%, above).</li><li>Military surplus SKS rifles with iron sights are not tack drivers. Many owners report groups of several inches at 100 m (Tip, owner reports; test yours).</li><li>Black tailed bucks weigh 48 to 90 kg, smaller than mule deer (90%, BC (British Columbia) deer account, via the <a href=\"#/s/mc-mule-deer-01/4\">mule deer Masterclass</a>).</li><li>Harrison and Fraser Valley deer country is thick second growth and clearcut edges. A 150 m limit covers most chances (Tip).</li></ul><aside class=\"callout lean\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">My lean (opinion)</div><p>My lean: the Tikka .308 is your deer rifle. The SKS is a fine backup or a thick timber rifle inside 100 m, after a gunsmith check and a zero with soft points.</p></aside></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 290\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A paper target with a 15 cm (6 inch) paper plate and a 5 shot group inside it at 100 m. If all 5 shots land inside, that distance is within your range.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"290\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The paper plate test (Tip)</text>\n<rect x=\"110.0\" y=\"50.0\" width=\"180.0\" height=\"180.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"200.0\" cy=\"140.0\" r=\"75.0\" fill=\"#F3E3D3\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"236.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\"></text><circle cx=\"186.0\" cy=\"130.0\" r=\"5.0\" fill=\"#17201A\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"212.0\" cy=\"122.0\" r=\"5.0\" fill=\"#17201A\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"204.0\" cy=\"154.0\" r=\"5.0\" fill=\"#17201A\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"180.0\" cy=\"158.0\" r=\"5.0\" fill=\"#17201A\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"222.0\" cy=\"146.0\" r=\"5.0\" fill=\"#17201A\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"254.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Plate 15 cm (6 in) at 100 m.</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"274.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5 shots inside? That is your range.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>5 shots, all in a 15 cm (6 in) plate at 100 m: OK to 100 m (Tip).</li><li>Miss the plate? Shorten your range until you do not (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how to run it</summary><ul><li>From a field rest you would use hunting: sitting with sticks, or kneeling against a tree (Tip). <a href=\"#/s/field-positions/0\">Field positions</a>.</li><li>Cold barrel first shot counts most. It is the one the deer gets (Tip).</li><li>Repeat at 150 m. Pass both or keep your limit at 100 m (Tip).</li><li>Placement: <a href=\"#/s/shot-placement/0\">shot placement</a>. Heart and lungs, broadside or quartering away <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout warn\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"BC deer rules for the SKS: centrefire rifle legal for deer; no minimum calibre in the table; no full metal jacket, expanding bullets only; magazine 5 maximum by federal law; loaded in a vehicle is illegal; no lights and no night shooting; no rifles on the Harrison Mills flats.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">SKS for deer: BC checklist</text>\n<circle cx=\"30.0\" cy=\"58.0\" r=\"9.9\" fill=\"#2E7D4F\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M25.5 58.0 l3.6 3.6 l6.3 -7.2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"50.0\" y=\"63.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Centrefire rifle: legal for deer</text><circle cx=\"30.0\" cy=\"89.0\" r=\"9.9\" fill=\"#2E7D4F\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M25.5 89.0 l3.6 3.6 l6.3 -7.2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"50.0\" y=\"94.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">No minimum calibre in the table</text><circle cx=\"30.0\" cy=\"120.0\" r=\"9.9\" fill=\"#B3261E\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"25.9\" y1=\"116.0\" x2=\"34.0\" y2=\"124.0\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"116.0\" x2=\"25.9\" y2=\"124.0\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"50.0\" y=\"125.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">No FMJ: expanding bullets only</text><circle cx=\"30.0\" cy=\"151.0\" r=\"9.9\" fill=\"#2E7D4F\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M25.5 151.0 l3.6 3.6 l6.3 -7.2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"50.0\" y=\"156.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Magazine 5 max (federal law)</text><circle cx=\"30.0\" cy=\"182.0\" r=\"9.9\" fill=\"#B3261E\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"25.9\" y1=\"177.9\" x2=\"34.0\" y2=\"186.1\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"177.9\" x2=\"25.9\" y2=\"186.1\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"50.0\" y=\"187.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Loaded in a vehicle: illegal</text><circle cx=\"30.0\" cy=\"213.0\" r=\"9.9\" fill=\"#B3261E\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"25.9\" y1=\"208.9\" x2=\"34.0\" y2=\"217.1\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"208.9\" x2=\"25.9\" y2=\"217.1\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"50.0\" y=\"218.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">No lights, no night shooting</text><circle cx=\"30.0\" cy=\"244.0\" r=\"9.9\" fill=\"#B3261E\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"25.9\" y1=\"239.9\" x2=\"34.0\" y2=\"248.1\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"239.9\" x2=\"25.9\" y2=\"248.1\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"50.0\" y=\"249.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">No rifles: Harrison Mills flats</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"288.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Study aid only. The regulations are the law.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Centrefire rifle: legal for deer. No calibre minimum in the table <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Expanding bullets only. No full metal jacket <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the rules, with sources</summary><ul><li>Deer: \"centrefire rifle, an air rifle of .35 calibre or larger, a 20 gauge or larger shotgun with No. 1 Buck or larger, or bow class B, C or D\" (99%, synopsis page 13, <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods/0\">Rule Book: legal methods</a>). The table sets no minimum calibre for centrefire rifles (95%, my reading).</li><li>No full metal jacket, tracer, incendiary or explosive bullets for hunting (99%, page 12).</li><li>No firearm with an electronically controlled firing mechanism, and no long gun with a barrel under 305 mm (99%, page 12). Your 520 mm barrel is fine.</li><li>The BC synopsis has no special rule for semi automatic rifles. The magazine plug rule is for shotguns only (95%, my reading of page 12).</li><li>The 5 round magazine limit is federal law (99%, SOR/98-462 Part 4, see <a href=\"#/s/mc-sks-08/2\">chapter 8</a>).</li><li>No round in the chamber or attached magazine in or on a vehicle (99%, page 11 item 28; <a href=\"#/s/mc-sks-03/3\">chapter 3</a>).</li><li>No lights to hunt by; hunting hours apply (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods/0\">Rule Book</a>).</li><li>Harrison Mills and Nicomen lowland: no rifles (99%, Closed Areas Regulation, via <a href=\"#/s/local-harrison-deer/0\">your Harrison deer hunt</a>).</li><li>Your licence, deer species licence and tags: <a href=\"#/s/licences/0\">licences</a>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Example</th><th>Price (CAD)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Entry</td><td>PPU or Sellier and Bellot 123 to 124 gr soft point</td><td><span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span></td></tr><tr><td>Mid</td><td>Hornady 123 gr SST</td><td>$41.99 per 20 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Premium</td><td>No confirmed Canadian listing</td><td><span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Price checked 2026-10-23. Rangeview Sports listing, shown out of stock <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Buy one box of each candidate. Hunt with the one that groups best (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: ammunition notes</summary><ul><li>Soft point and polymer tip bullets expand. That is what the law asks for (99%, page 12).</li><li>Steel cased soft points exist and work in most SKS rifles (Tip). Check the box says non corrosive.</li><li>Zero with the exact load you hunt with (<a href=\"#/s/mc-sks-04/5\">chapter 4</a>) <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>US prices seen for the same loads were about 20 to 35 US dollars per 20 (65%, US retailer listings, 2026-10-23). Canadian prices run higher. <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> at a Fraser Valley shop.</li><li>More on choosing ammunition: <a href=\"#/s/ammo-guide/0\">ammo guide</a>.</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout rule\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom): Know your rifle's distance. Then cut it by a quarter for the deer.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Taking a 250 m shot because the leaf says 1000.</li><li>Hunting with surplus full metal jacket.</li><li>Zeroing with one load and hunting with another.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Run the plate test at 100 and 150 m with your soft points. Write your limit on tape on the stock.</p></aside>","<ul><li>Hornady 7.62x39 123 gr SST ballistics, via <a href=\"https://www.midwestgunworks.com/page/mgwi/prod/80784\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Midwest Gun Works</a> and <a href=\"https://www.kygunco.com/product/hornady-80784-7.62-x-39-123-gr-sst-black-2350-fps-20-pack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KYGUNCO</a> listings, checked 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></li><li>Hunt Mentor <a href=\"#/s/ballistics-308/0\">.308 ballistics</a> (Federal data) (75 to 85%)</li><li>US Army, <a href=\"https://archive.org/download/gunmanual_sksmanual/sksmanual.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TC 9-56 (October 1969)</a>, technical data <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></li><li>BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028, pages 11 to 13, via the <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods/0\">Rule Book</a> <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www.rangeviewsports.ca/?p=163977\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Rangeview Sports</a>, Hornady 7.62x39 123 gr SST, $41.99, price checked 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li></ul>"]